  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $A$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $A$ where every element of $A$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{0,4,8,\u2026,36},{40,44,48,\u2026,76},{80}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{0,8,12},{16,20,\u2026,80}}$ is not a partition because the element $4$ does not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${\u2205,{0},{4,8,12,\u2026,80}}$ is not a partition because the subset $\u2205$ is empty.\n\n- ${{0,2,4,\u2026,40},{44,46,\u2026,80}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $2$) that do not appear in $A.$\n\n- ${{0,8,16\u2026,40},{48,56,\u2026,80}}$ is not a partition because many elements of $A$ (such as $4$)  do not appear in any subsets.",
